.TH ECHO 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
echo \- display a line of text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo
.RB [ \-n ]
.RI [ word ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B echo
writes its
.IR word s
to standard output, separated by single spaces, followed by a new line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Do not write the trailing new line.
Only a first argument of
.B \-n
is taken as the option; anywhere else it is a word.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
echo hello world
echo \-n "no new line"
echo $PATH
.fi
.SH NOTES
.B echo
is a program, not a shell builtin.
It does not interpret backslash escapes, and has no
.B \-e
or
.BR \-E .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR cat (1)
